From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] rockchip: rk3399: nova: keep the stock U-Boot's boot
 logo on the panel

Copyright (C) 2026 Olympian LED, Inc.

Rigol's stock U-Boot draws the boot logo into DRAM and leaves the display
controller scanning it out when it starts this U-Boot. In the FDT it passes
in x0 it names that framebuffer, as the reg of the reserved-memory node
compatible with "rockchip,drm-logo", and describes the picture in each
display route (/display-subsystem/route/<route>: logo,offset, logo,width,
logo,height, logo,bpp, logo,ymirror, the video,* timings and the overscan,*
margins). Booting a kernel itself, it writes the same into the kernel's DTB;
the kernel's display driver then reserves that memory, maps it 1:1 for the
display controller's IOMMU and takes the picture over.

The chainload boots the FIT's own DTB, whose drm-logo reg is empty and whose
routes carry none of it. So the kernel reserved nothing there, used the
framebuffer as free memory, and its display driver had no logo to take over:
the panel showed the logo garbled, then a full screen of stripes, then black,
until NovaOS drew its own splash. And this U-Boot relocated to the top of
RAM, into the 32 MiB the stock U-Boot sets aside for the logo, clear of the
picture only because the picture is small and at the start of that area.

Now:
- arch_setup_dest_addr keeps the relocated U-Boot (image, malloc, stacks,
  page tables) below the logo x0 names, as it keeps the previous stage's FDT
  and initrd;
- `nova boot` keeps the logo out of lmb, so bootm places nothing there, and
  takes a copy of x0;
- ft_board_setup, for a NovaOS FIT only, writes x0's drm-logo reg into the
  kernel's drm-logo node and every property of each x0 route the kernel's
  route of the same name lacks or holds differently, except the route's
  phandle, its connection and its status, which stay the booted DTB's.

A kexec entry has no logo of the stock U-Boot's on the panel: it hands over
nothing, and the FDT it gives a slot's U-Boot names no logo. The stock
firmware's rung is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
---
 board/rigol/nova_rk3399/nova_rk3399.c   | 200 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 board/rigol/nova_rk3399/nova_rk3399.env |   5 +-
 2 files changed, 202 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/board/rigol/nova_rk3399/nova_rk3399.c b/board/rigol/nova_rk3399/nova_rk3399.c
index 24ed580f..a64f7b06 100644
--- a/board/rigol/nova_rk3399/nova_rk3399.c
+++ b/board/rigol/nova_rk3399/nova_rk3399.c
@@ -482,6 +482,51 @@ static __maybe_unused u64 fdt_chosen_u64(const void *fdt, const char *name)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The boot logo on the panel: the stock U-Boot draws it into DRAM, leaves the display controller
+ * scanning it out, and names that framebuffer in its FDT as the reg of the reserved-memory node
+ * compatible with "rockchip,drm-logo" (the kernel's display driver takes the picture over from
+ * there). That node, a child of /reserved-memory (where the DT spec puts every reserved region),
+ * and its parent in *parent. Looked up below /reserved-memory, not by a scan of the whole tree:
+ * scans of a 100 KB tree cost milliseconds here, in every boot.
+ */
+static int nova_logo_node(const void *fdt, int *parent)
+{
+	int node;
+
+	*parent = fdt_path_offset(fdt, "/reserved-memory");
+	if (*parent < 0)
+		return *parent;
+	fdt_for_each_subnode(node, fdt, *parent)
+		if (!fdt_node_check_compatible(fdt, node, "rockchip,drm-logo"))
+			return node;
+	return -FDT_ERR_NOTFOUND;
+}
+
+/*
+ * The logo's range, or -1 when the FDT names none (an empty reg: no logo drawn) or one outside
+ * RAM.
+ */
+static int nova_logo_range(const void *fdt, u64 *base, u64 *size)
+{
+	int parent, node = nova_logo_node(fdt, &parent);
+	int ac, sc, len;
+	const fdt32_t *reg;
+
+	if (node < 0)
+		return -1;
+	ac = fdt_address_cells(fdt, parent);
+	sc = fdt_size_cells(fdt, parent);
+	reg = fdt_getprop(fdt, node, "reg", &len);
+	if (!reg || ac < 1 || ac > 2 || sc < 1 || sc > 2 || len < (ac + sc) * 4)
+		return -1;
+	*base = fdt_read_number(reg, ac);
+	*size = fdt_read_number(reg + ac, sc);
+	if (!*size || *base < gd->ram_base || *base + *size > gd->ram_top)
+		return -1;
+	return 0;
+}
+
